// ora-mod-cm — generated by tools/merge.js: src/ora-mod-cm-*.js plus matching questions from the Oracle role banks (tools/modules.js).
QB['ora-mod-cm'] = (QB['ora-mod-cm'] || []).concat([["Banking","Design the bank integration architecture for a multinational using Oracle Fusion.","- Options: **direct host-to-host** per bank, **SWIFT** (Alliance Lite2 / service bureau), or a **bank connectivity hub** (e.g. Kyriba, a bank-agnostic gateway).\n- **Formats**: ISO 20022 (pain.001 payments, pain.002 status, camt.053/052 statements) to reduce bank-specific work.\n- **Security**: PGP encryption/signing, SFTP keys, segregation of payment release.\n- **Flows**: payment files from PPRs → hub → banks; acknowledgments and statements back into Cash Management.\n- **Treasury** functions (in-house bank, netting) possibly in a TMS integrated with Fusion.\n- **Monitoring** of file transmission and acknowledgments.","D"],["Banking","How do you design payment controls to prevent fraud?","- **Segregation**: supplier bank maintenance ≠ invoice entry ≠ payment release.\n- **Bank account change verification** with callback and approval.\n- **Payment approval** for PPRs above thresholds (or all PPRs).\n- **Positive pay** for checks; **payee name match** services.\n- **File security**: encrypted, signed files; no manual file editing; transmission automated.\n- **Monitoring**: new bank accounts paid for the first time, payments outside normal patterns.","D"],["Cash Management","How does bank statement reconciliation work in Oracle Cash Management?","- **Load bank statements** — electronic files (BAI2, MT940, CAMT.053) or manual entry.\n- **Autoreconciliation** matches statement lines to system transactions (AP payments, AR receipts, journals) using **reconciliation rule sets** — match on reference, amount, date with tolerances.\n- **Manual reconciliation** for what auto-match misses.\n- **External transactions** — create bank charges or interest directly from unmatched lines, using transaction creation rules.\n- Reconciled payments clear (Dr Cash Clearing, Cr Cash) and accounting goes to GL.","B"],["Cash Management","What is the difference between a bank, a branch and a bank account in Oracle?","- **Bank** — the institution (e.g. JPMorgan Chase).\n- **Branch** — a specific branch with routing number/BIC.\n- **Bank account** — your company's account at that branch: account number, currency, GL cash and cash clearing accounts, and usage (Payables, Receivables, Payroll).\n\nBank accounts are owned by a **legal entity** and can be used by the business units granted access.","B"],["Cash Management","How would you design bank statement processing for 200 bank accounts across 15 banks?","- **Standard formats**: CAMT.053 or BAI2 from every bank where possible; avoid custom parsers.\n- **Automated retrieval** via SFTP/bank connectivity, scheduled **Load and Import Bank Statement**.\n- **Reconciliation rule sets** per account type (disbursement, collection, payroll, zero balance).\n- **Transaction creation rules** for fees and interest.\n- **Exception dashboards** for unreconciled items by age.\n- Prior-day and **intraday** statements for cash positioning.\n- Ownership: treasury vs shared services for exceptions.","D"],["Cash Management","How do you design reconciliation rule sets for high auto-match rates?","- Analyze the bank statements: what references does the bank pass (check number, payment reference, invoice number)?\n- Build rules from **strictest to loosest**: exact reference + amount → amount + date tolerance → one-to-many and many-to-one for batch deposits.\n- Add **tolerance rules** for small differences (bank fees) and **transaction creation rules** for recurring charges (fees, interest).\n- Make sure payment references sent to the bank are returned on statements (e.g. ISO 20022 end-to-end ID).\n- Measure and refine the auto-match rate monthly.","D"],["Cash Management","What is cash positioning and forecasting in Fusion?","- **Cash positioning** shows the daily cash position by bank account/currency: opening balance + expected inflows (AR receipts, receipts) − outflows (AP payments, payroll).\n- **Cash forecasting** projects cash for future periods from AP, AR, POs, sales orders, payroll and external sources.\n- Uses bank statement balances and subledger data.\n- Treasury uses it to plan funding, investments and intercompany transfers.\n\nMany large companies use dedicated treasury systems (Kyriba, etc.) alongside Oracle.","D"],["Cash Management","How do you handle bank charges and interest in reconciliation?","- Use **transaction creation rules**: when a statement line matches a pattern (e.g. bank code for fees), Oracle creates an **external cash transaction** with the right account automatically.\n- Then autoreconcile those lines.\n- Review created transactions before close.","D"]]);
